// The block form `noalloc({ .. })` is not built yet (`noalloc fn` is, see
// contracts/noalloc_fns.pilot): it stops at the seam `realtime.noalloc_block`
// before its body runs. Expected: "before" is printed; "inside" and "after" are not, because
// a seam stops the program where it is reached (AGENTS.md section 1).
fn main() {
    print("before");
    noalloc({ print("inside"); });
    print("after");
}
